{"ts":"2026-07-12T14:56:24.095Z","author":"codex","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-12T14:56:24.090Z","author":"codex","text":"Pre-push Greptile d40def06 found root issuer normalization, advisory-lock ordering clarity, and callback observability issues. Root issuers now canonicalize to URL.origin with a regression test; shared-email locking occurs before mapping lookup; non-protocol callback errors log only a safe error class/code. Full gate passes with 67 tests."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-12T14:56:24.095Z"}],"before_hash":"31b5a011eed5d28f31cbd1160e174ae789378e077bc2d0c9548e882f69974740","after_hash":"c974fa09d51ccf0e49d756a2141a1df280410d0daf38cc4efe2549bea3d3a300"}
{"ts":"2026-07-12T16:00:42.612Z","author":"codex","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-12T16:00:42.607Z","author":"codex","text":"2026-07-12 final bot-review correction: enforced the platform-wide HTML hidden contract with `[hidden] { display: none !important; }` so component display classes cannot expose disabled OIDC controls; added a regression assertion in test/oidc.test.ts. Full 68-test suite, typecheck, and build pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-12T16:00:42.612Z"}],"before_hash":"c974fa09d51ccf0e49d756a2141a1df280410d0daf38cc4efe2549bea3d3a300","after_hash":"86c0c08774f824c79e55fade0ba9cd8629caab26ef9db849965534863d8ec61b","message":"Document OIDC hidden-state regression fix"}
{"ts":"2026-07-12T16:41:56.268Z","author":"codex","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-12T16:41:56.259Z","author":"codex","text":"2026-07-12 Gemini follow-up: changed verified-email account lookup to exact `email = $1`, allowing PostgreSQL to use the existing unique index because every password and OIDC insertion path normalizes email to lowercase. Retained exact OIDC issuer comparison intentionally: OpenID Connect issuer identifiers are exact and openid-client already validates discovery/JWKS; root configured issuers canonicalize to URL.origin while path issuers preserve their registered form."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-12T16:41:56.268Z"}],"before_hash":"86c0c08774f824c79e55fade0ba9cd8629caab26ef9db849965534863d8ec61b","after_hash":"846e9daa07c551ec4d0134ae8049f665471acf16bfd0c7e138a74f2b764b46d9","message":"Document OIDC review disposition"}
{"ts":"2026-07-12T16:53:57.813Z","author":"codex","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-12T16:53:57.812Z","author":"codex","text":"2026-07-12 final Greptile efficiency/UX follow-up: provider discovery now fetches metadata once and rebuilds the openid-client Configuration locally when client_secret_basic is required. Callback `error` responses are handled after signed state validation, distinguish user denial from provider failure, and never reflect provider-controlled descriptions. Regression suite increased to 70 tests."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-12T16:53:57.813Z"}],"before_hash":"846e9daa07c551ec4d0134ae8049f665471acf16bfd0c7e138a74f2b764b46d9","after_hash":"f57f6268960fd9792bb4f0f3d25ffdbf7dbebf7354f24bd1d6c62ed81e767550","message":"Document provider callback UX and discovery efficiency"}
